# Routing only. No credential: qits-artifacts requires and reads none, in either direction, and an
# install needs nothing at all — only `npm publish` has a client-side pre-flight, and nothing here
# publishes.
#
# localhost:8081 is the local platform's host-published qits-artifacts port. It is the right
# address twice over: a developer on the deployment host dials it directly, and so does the
# `pnpm install` inside docker/Dockerfile, because the image is built on that same host's daemon
# with `--network=host` (see the Dockerfile and .config/qits/ci-post-receive.yml).
#
# CI overwrites this file's effect rather than editing it: the pipeline writes ~/.npmrc from
# $QITS_NPM_PROXY_URL / $QITS_NPM_REGISTRY_URL — the qits-net aliases (qits-artifacts:8080) — and
# passes it with --userconfig so it outranks this project file inside the step container.
registry=http://localhost:8081/artifacts/npm/npmjs/
@qits:registry=http://localhost:8081/artifacts/npm/npm/
